op7t-0201: cameras, step 1: a read-only survey of the rear main sensor's power, clocks and pins

2026-11-12, user: camera next. Before switching anything on, read what the
rear main sensor (live DT qcom,cam-sensor@0) depends on and in what state ABL
left it, so the power-up (step 2) is built on facts:
- GCC camera clocks (ahb/hf axi/sf axi/xo);
- TLMM config of its pins: gpio11 CAM_VANA_0, gpio14 MCLK1, gpio17-20 CCI
  (master 1 = 19/20), gpio29 CAM_VANA2_0, gpio30 CAM_RESET0;
- PMIC over SPMI (reads only; sweet_spmi.c's allowlist widened): PM8150L
  L1 (cam_vio), 0xa0 (BOB?), GPIO1 (CAM_PVDD); PM8009 L1 (cam_vdig);
- cmd-db entries of the RPMh rails ldoc1 (XOB), bobc1, ldof1 (new
  sweet_rpmh_describe: no vote, no type check);
- the camera clock controller (only if GCC's camera AHB is on): TITAN_TOP
  GDSC, gdsc/core ahb/cpas ahb/camnoc axi, MCLK1, CCI0/1, slow ahb, PLL0/2;
- CCI0's version register only if its power domain and clocks already run.
Offsets from Linux camcc-sm8150.c, gcc-sm8150.c, pinctrl-sm8150.c,
i2c-qcom-cci.c. `sysctl kern.sweetcam=1`, report in kern.sweetcamlog.
Not compiled locally (no compiler for the kernel here): the CI build is the
check.

Apply after 0200.
---
